A photo of a notebook sketch is enough to start. Circuit Diagram Generator redraws the idea as a standards-correct schematic you can edit by hand or refine with AI.

## When sketch import shines

- Classroom whiteboards before the next period
- Coffee-shop napkin designs you do not want to redraw
- Legacy diagrams sitting only on paper

## How to get a good capture

- Shoot square-on with even lighting — avoid heavy shadows.
- Keep component labels readable when possible.
- Crop tightly around the circuit.

## After import

Review footprints and nets, run a quick simulation, then export for documentation or CAD. The sketch is a starting point — the editable schematic is the deliverable.

[Open the studio](https://app.circuitdiagramgenerator.ai/) and try uploading a sketch.
